[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_1]
A Small Diner

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_1_desc]
The Stratusburg was even quieter at night than during the day. Under moonlight, the already sparsely populated Stratusburg seemed even more desolate. However, there was one exception — a small diner across from the town hall, where the lights were on.
Although the diner was only a few years old, it had already become a local tradition for the residents of Stratusburg to gather here at night. The owners of the diner become quite wealthy — at least by Stratusburg standards: even the largest commercial empire established in this small town could not compare to a small company on the streets of Manehattan or Las Pegasus.
The founders of the diner were childhood friends, Sky Stinger and Vapor Trail, the only pair of outstanding fliers in the town for decades. When they were both admitted to the Wonderbolts Academy, all residents of the town had taken three days off to celebrate. The residents celebrated the rare geniuses for decades, believing that they would finally change Stratusburg. Unfortunately, the good times did not last long. After the war ended, the Wonderbolts were forced to disband, and Sky Stinger and Vapor Trail had to return to Stratusburg. Unemployed, they opened a small diner here.
During the most turbulent times of the autonomy movement, the diner did not participate, but tacitly allowed it to become a base for the autonomy movement. On the night of Spitfire’s victory, most of the residents came to the diner to celebrate their victory. Since then, the diner has become a popular meeting place for the residents of Stratusburg, where they gather, chat, drink, and even engage in small-scale gambling and illegal flying competitions.
Perhaps, this is the curse of Stratusburg — nothing big ever happens here, and there are no great heroes or villains. Even a few talented fliers can only eventually live an ordinary life in this small town. But is this really a bad thing? While the ponies of Equestria are at war with their own kind, living in turmoil and fear, Stratusburg seems to be in a different world. The residents here are united and harmonious, and except when necessary they take to the streets to protest the Empire’s tyranny and defend their autonomy, most of the time they are just singing and dancing together in the diner, as if all difficulties can wait until tomorrow.

At this moment, Spitfire, who had just finished her shift, arrived at the diner from the town hall. As soon as she entered the diner, the residents began to cheer and toast. When the residents quieted down, Spitfire smiled and said to everyone:
“I’m happy to tell you all! This time, Stratusburg has once again secured our 3% share from the Empire’s subsidy to Cloudsdale!”
“Great! You know the drill, the diner is on the house tonight! Cheers!” Sky Stinger raised his glass first.
“Cheers!” All the ponies in the diner raised their glasses together.

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_1_o0]
Cheers!

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_2]
Rumor Rustle

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_2_desc]
At dusk, the special agent of the EEMO, Rumor Rustle, walked into the diner across from the town hall of Stratusburg. He ordered a plate of muffins and a glass of apple cider, then sat down in the corner of the diner.
When the sun completely disappeared from the horizon, there were already many ponies in the diner. They had finished their meals and were chatting, watching the news, or playing cards in the diner. After drinking a few more glasses of apple cider, Rumor Rustle mingled in the conversation of these ponies.
Pretending to be heavily drunk, he said with a long drawl, “... Eh, have you guys heard? I heard, burp~ that Cozy Glow, she recently, recently wants to recruit soldiers in Stratusburg again.” The crowd booed.
He continued, “Yeah! Isn’t it funny?... Hey! But anyway, don’t tell anyone, I heard, I heard that this time the recruitment is quite generous! I have a friend, uh, he got, he got, he got a whole bag of gold coins!” After speaking, Rumor Rustle was laughing inside, this should attract the attention of some ponies.
Rumor Rustle knew that this is the liveliest place in Stratusburg, and one sentence is enough to change the thoughts of the entire town.

The next day, the number of visitors to the Equestria Empire’s Stratusburg recruitment office remained zero.

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_2_o0]
Damn, why isn’t it working?

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_3]
Military Pressure

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_3_desc]
An imperial officer gets off his palanquin, smoking a pipe, and heads towards the city hall of Stratusburg. Behind him are a dozen soldiers holding guns. When he reaches the door, the guards stop him. The officer looks at them displeasedly, “Can’t you see who I am? Call Spitfire, let her come down, now.”
“We know you are an imperial officer, but Stratusburg is an autonomous territory. You can’t enter at will. Do you have an appointment?” A Stratusburg guard says firmly.
The officer is very dissatisfied. He raises his hoof, and in an instant, dozens of soldiers under his command raise their guns, pointing them at the guards. The guards face the muzzles without flinching, standing straight and continuing to block the officer.

At this moment, Spitfire walks out from the balcony on the second floor, looking down at the imperial officer, “I am an empire-appointed dominion governer. If you want to talk, call Cozy Glow or Fancy Pants and let them talk to me. You guys are not high enough in rank.”
The imperial officer looks at Spitfire, his face darkening, “Huh, Stratusburg, this small place, really thinks highly of itself. Spitfire, you are aware of the conscription matter, you know why I’m here. The empire hasn’t made any demands for so many years, but you’ve been taking the empire’s financial subsidies.”
Spitfire turns around and doesn’t even look at the officer anymore, “Tell your soldiers to put down their guns first. Even if it’s the imperial army, if they shoot in our dominion’s autonomous territory, we have the right to lawfully shoot you dead.”
Hearing this, the officer sneers, “Stratusburg is just relying on the empire’s love for peace and can’t be bothered with you. Now that it’s wartime, if you don’t listen, we don’t mind blowing up this little trash burg. Spitfire, I’ll warn you in case you don’t know, I’ve arranged for three imperial divisions at the border. As soon as I give the order, they will immediately attack. How long can you resist this small place? Even if we don’t start a war but siege for three months, you will have to surrender.”

Hearing this, Spitfire turns back to look at the officer, helplessly saying, “Indeed, we can’t resist for long. How many troops do you want to conscript? You know we don’t have many ponies in this little trash burg.”
Seeing Spitfire’s attitude soften, the officer immediately puts on a smug posture, “The empire wants an attitude. Whether it’s ten ponies or twenty ponies, I must take a batch with me today.”
Spitfire suddenly laughs and responds, “Alright, I’ll report to the Empress now. I’ll say that during the war, the officer transferred three imperial divisions away from the front line without authorization for three months and successfully conscripted twenty ponies for the army?”

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_3_o0]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_4]
Invitation Letter

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_4_desc]
The officer came to Stratusburg again, and as soon as he got off the car, he walked angrily to the door of the city hall. Before the guard could speak, he directly slapped a piece of paper on the guard’s face, “Do you have eyes? Can you see it? Here! The Empress’s signature! Can I enter, huh? Can I enter now?”
The guard didn’t say anything, made way, and the officer walked in. He saw Spitfire at the table, “Spitfire, this time it’s an invitation letter issued by the Empress herself, asking you to go to the palace to discuss the conscription.”
After speaking, the officer muttered, “Huh! This kind of small trash burg shouldn’t even have the qualification to meet the Empress.”
Spitfire was writing documents at the table, and without looking up, she said, “Alright, mailpony, thank you. Put the invitation letter on the table, I will go. Close the door before you leave.”

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_4_o0]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_5]
From Stratusburg to Canterlot

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_5_desc]
The train is slowly entering Canterlot. Spitfire, sitting by the window of the special carriage, feels a little nervous but not flustered.
Spitfire is well aware that the Empress’s invitation this time is not for a meeting but a trap. Before leaving Stratusburg, Spitfire had issued a notice to all residents, telling them that she would go to Canterlot. If she couldn’t come back, then the uprising would immediately break out and couldn’t be stopped until the last resident of Stratusburg was killed by the imperial army. This is Stratusburg’s secret weapon — unity. Spitfire trusts the residents of Stratusburg. She believes they will stick to their position. This deterrence of resistance to the end is enough to make the imperial army hesitate.
What does the Empire want? The Empire doesn’t need the resources of Stratusburg or conscription in Stratusburg. What the Empire needs is an example, a demonstration, proof that the Empire has the ability to control and coerce its territories to act according to the central will. On the one hoof, this means that if necessary, the Empire will carry out its deterrence to the end. Otherwise, Stratusburg’s refusal to the Empire will become an object for other territories to follow. But on the other hoof, this also means that Stratusburg’s weak deterrence becomes strong: even if Stratusburg is sure to lose, if Stratusburg fight the army of the Empire to the last moment, the cost and public opinion impact will be unbearable for the Empire.
So, as long as the cost of the conflict is unacceptable to both sides, this is a game of hawks and doves, a game of the brave. The reason why Spitfire firmly believes that Stratusburg will win is also obvious — Spitfire is more determined than Cozy Glow, the residents of Stratusburg are more united and braver than the Empire’s government. This is enough to make the small Stratusburg an equal counterpart to the monstrous Empire.

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_5_o0]
Then Let’s Talk

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_6]
The Game of the Brave

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_6_desc]
“Spitfire, you should have read the document delivered by the ‘mailpony’ of the Imperial Army, right?” The Empress asked as Spitfire walked into the room, without waiting for her to present her souvenirs from Stratusburg to the Empress.
“Yes, Your Majesty. So you should also have read the notice I issued in Stratusburg before I left, right?” Spitfire smiled slightly and put the special product from her bag aside.

“I have read it,” the Empress nodded, “Your notice is very interesting, ‘During the war, the residents of Stratusburg should fully support the Equestria Empire. If any imperial deserters are found in Stratusburg, the residents of Stratusburg should intercept them to the death and capture them all for Her Majesty.’ Quite funny, right? ‘Imperial deserters’?” The Empress asked ironically.
“Your Majesty, the main point of the notice is ‘the residents of Stratusburg should fully support the Equestria Empire’. You don’t need to think too much about it.” Spitfire nodded and smiled, “I believe the residents of Stratusburg will stick to their position, not disappoint Your Majesty’s expectations, and eliminate every deserter until the last moment.”
“Very good! Stratusburg is so loyal. I am considering making Stratusburg completely independent from the Empire after the war!” Cozy Glow tentatively said, looking at Spitfire’s reaction. Spitfire responded quickly, “How could we want to be independent from the wise rule of Your Majesty? You see, it is Your Majesty’s protection that has saved us from the suffering of war. Until now, no pony from Stratusburg has been sent to the battlefield.”

Seeing Spitfire continue to be sarcastic, Cozy Glow the Empress changed the subject, “Oh, by the way, Spitfire, I don’t know if you have heard any rumors in your small diner in Stratusburg. The treatment of conscription in the Empire is going to be improved again. Every soldier can get a whole cart of gold coins.” Then, she leaned over to Spitfire and whispered, “Actually, it’s not just for the soldiers. Do you know that every autonomous territory with outstanding conscription will get a hefty reward for the governer? Do you think this is a good opportunity?”
“Your Majesty,” Spitfire looked at Cozy Glow, “I serve as the governer of the autonomous territory because the residents of Stratusburg trust me and believe that I will serve the Empire wholeheartedly, for your Majesty, not for money.”
“Yes, Spitfire, you are right.” Bribery failed, so Cozy Glow continued, “But these rewards are not just for the governer. I am considering raising the subsidy ratio of Stratusburg to 7%. Spitfire, what do you think of this proposal? Or 10%?”
“Your Majesty,” Spitfire shook her head again, “Stratusburg is relatively small, and what it lacks most is the labor force. The conscription affects our contribution to the Empire’s construction cause, which cannot be compensated by a few percents of the subsidy.”

“Let’s not talk about this for now,” the Empress’s tone revealed her suppressed anger, “You are invited to this meeting by me, so I will protect your safety. But the current situation is very dangerous. You should be careful. You know, maybe one day, in Stratusburg, something unexpected will happen. Like you being assassinated by the Resistance.”
Spitfire heard the Empress’s meaning but still smiled and replied, “Thank you for your concern! I will carry weapons with me to protect my safety. Even if I accident happen to me, my comrades from the ‘Free Stratusburg’ will quickly find out the murderer and make them pay. An eye for an eye, a tooth for a tooth, this is our principle. Even the ‘Resistance’ in Canterlot will not be an exception.” With that, Spitfire straightened her clothes and inadvertently revealed the weapons in her side bag — although they had been checked by the Empire, this still made the Empress subconsciously take a few steps back.

Cozy Glow’s fright was obviously seen, she fell silent for a long time, took a sip of tea to calm down, “Spitfire. You can go now.”
“Thank you, Your Majesty. So... conclusion about the conscription?” Spitfire continued to pat her side bag.
“Stratusburg not only doesn’t need conscription, I will also reward your loyalty,” Cozy Glow the Empress said tremblingly, “Cart of gold coins for the Mayor, Stratusburg’s subsidy, and independence after the war, I will give them all to you.”

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_6_o0]
“Eh?” Even Spitfire was a little surprised.

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_7]
From Canterlot to Stratusburg

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_7_desc]
Spitfire left, and a secret door in the Empress’s room opened. Cozy Glow walked out of the shadow, clapping his hooves and praising, “What a wonderful performance, Empress, you are so amazing!”
Cozy Glow also returned to her original arrogant appearance, “It’s your script, Fancy Pants, I just performed according to your script. But, are you sure this will work?”

At night, the sound of celebration in the small diner opposite Stratusburg was almost enough to lift the roof. The residents had already prepared for the worst — Spitfire might not come back alive, and Stratusburg would have a direct conflict with the imperial army. Now, not only was there no conflict, but Stratusburg also received a lot of benefits from the Empire, including a 7% increase in subsidies and independent status after the war. All of this was thanks to Spitfire, and the residents of Stratusburg were celebrating Spitfire’s victory.
Rumor Rustle continued to sit in the corner drinking. When a pony sat down at his table, he would whisper, “I’m really curious, how did the great Spitfire do it? According to Spitfire’s own words, Cozy Glow’s attitude made a 180-degree turn and completely agreed to all her conditions. How is that possible? I heard rumors that Cozy Glow gave Spitfire some individual benefits, carts of gold coins, they are now parked behind the city hall. There are also rumors that Cozy Glow gave a 10% subsidy, not 7%, and the remaining 3% seems to be what Spitfire requested for herself. Do you think this is true?”
Rumor Rustle knew that this is the liveliest place in Stratusburg, and one sentence is enough to change the thoughts of the entire town.

[en.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_7_o0]
Sharing hardships is easy, sharing happiness is hard

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_1]
小餐馆

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_1_desc]
入夜的层云堡，比白天时更加寂静。本就没有多少居民的层云堡，在月光的照耀下，显得更加空旷。不过，有一处例外——在市政厅对面的一间小餐馆内，灯火通明。
尽管餐馆才新建几年，夜晚聚集在在这已经成为了层云堡的民间习俗。这家小餐馆也赚的盆满钵满——当然也仅限于层云堡角度来说：即使在这种小镇子上建立最大的商业帝国，也比不上马哈顿或者洛马基街边一家平平无奇的小公司。
餐馆的创办者是一对青梅竹马的好友，破空与雾轨，他们是这个小镇几十年来仅有的一对出色飞马。当他们都考入闪电天马学院时，镇上的居民曾经全部放假三天庆祝。镇民们庆祝着几十年少见的天才，以为他们将改变层云堡。只可惜好景不长，战争结束后，闪电天马队被迫解散，破空与雾轨也只能回到层云堡，失业的他们在这里开了一家小餐馆。
在自治运动闹得最凶的那段时间，餐馆虽没有参与，却也默许这里成为了自治运动的据点。而喷火获胜的当晚，小镇大半的居民都来到这家餐馆，庆祝他们的胜利。从那以后，这家餐馆就成了层云堡的民间会所，居民们在这里聚会、聊天、喝酒，甚至还有一些金额不大的赌博和非法飞行竞赛。
或许，这就是层云堡的诅咒吧——在这里，永远不会有什么大事发生，也不会有什么伟大的英雄或是邪恶的反派诞生。即使是有一两位天赋异禀的飞马，也一定只能在这座默默无闻的小城镇里度过平凡的一生。然而，这真的是件坏事么？在小马国的小马们与自己的同族战争，生活在动荡与恐惧中时，层云堡却似乎处在一个不同的世界。这里的居民们团结和睦，除了必要时会走上街头共同抗议帝国的暴政保卫自治，其他时候大多就像这样，在小餐馆里一起唱着歌跳着舞，仿佛一切困难都可以等到第二天再说。

就在这时，刚刚下了晚班的喷火从市政厅来到了小餐馆。一走进餐馆，民众们就开始欢呼、干杯。等民众安静下来，喷火笑着对大家说：
“很高兴地告诉大家！这次帝国拨给云中城的补贴，层云堡又争取到了3%！”
“好诶！老规矩，今晚餐馆全免单！干杯！” 破空首先举起了酒杯。
“干杯！” 餐馆里的所有小马一起干了一杯。

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_1_o0]
干杯！

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_2]
流言沙沙

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_2_desc]
黄昏，小马利亚帝国秩序部特工流言沙沙，走进了层云堡市政厅对面的餐馆。他点了一盘杯糕，一杯苹果汁，就在餐馆的角落里坐下来。
当太阳完全从地平线上消失时，餐馆内已经有不少小马，他们吃完了饭，在餐馆内聊天、看新闻或是打牌。又下肚了几杯苹果汁，流言沙沙混进了这些小马的谈话中。
装作醉醺醺的样子，他拖着长音说道：“...唔你们知道吗？我听说，嗝~ 和煦那个家伙，最近，最近又想来层云堡征兵了。” 群众中嘘声一片。
他紧接着说：“我就说，很搞笑吧？...诶！不过你别说，听说，听说这次征兵给的还挺多！我有个朋友，唔他拿，他拿，他拿到了整整一袋金币呢！” 说完，流言沙沙心中窃喜，这样应该就能引起一些小马的注意了。
流言沙沙知道这里是层云堡最热闹的地方，一句话，就足够改变整座城镇的思想。

第二天，小马利亚帝国的层云堡征兵处，访客数目依然为零。

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_2_o0]
混蛋，怎么会不管用？

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_3]
军事压力

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_3_desc]
一名帝国军官走下小轿，叼着烟斗，向着层云堡市政厅走去，身后是十几名持枪的士兵。当他走到门前，守卫拦住了他，军官不悦地看了看他们：“你们看不出来我是谁吗？叫喷火下来，现在。”
“我们知道您是帝国的军官，但层云堡是自治领，您不能随意进入。您有预约吗？” 一名层云堡守卫坚定地说道。
军官非常不满，举起蹄子，一瞬间，他手下的几十名士兵举起了枪，指向了守卫。守卫们面对着枪口，没有退缩，反而直起身子，继续挡在军官面前。

这时，喷火从二楼的阳台走了出来，居高临下地看着帝国军官：“我是帝国任命的自治领市长，想要谈的话，叫和煦或者花花短裤来找我，你们这些人，级别还不够。”
帝国军官看着喷火，脸色阴沉：“哈，层云堡这种小地方，还真把自己当回事了。征兵的事喷火你也早就知道了，你知道我是来干嘛的。这么多年了帝国都没有提出什么要求，你们却一直在拿着帝国的财政补贴。”
喷火转过身去，甚至不再看着军官：“叫你的士兵先把枪放下，即使是帝国军队，如果在自治领内开枪，我们也有权利依法击毙。”
听到这话，军官冷笑一声：“层云堡只不过是仗着帝国热爱和平，懒得管你们，现在是战争时期了，再不听话，我们不介意把这个小垃圾堡全部炸完。喷火，如果你还不知道，那我告诉你，我已经安排了三个帝国师在边境上，只要我一声令下，他们就会立即进攻，你们这个小地方，能抵挡多久？即使不爆发战争，包围你们三个月，你们也不得不投降。”

听到这话，喷火回过头来看着军官，无奈地说道：“那我们确实抵抗不了多久，你们要征多少兵？你也知道我们这个小垃圾堡没多少小马。”
看到喷火态度缓和，军官立马摆出得意的姿态：“帝国要的是态度，十只小马也好，二十只小马也好，但我今天必须要带走一批。”
喷火突然笑了出来，回应：“好，那我这就向女皇报告，说军官你在战争时期私自将三个帝国师调离前线三个月，成功征兵小马二十只？”

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_3_o0]
额...

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_4]
邀请函

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_4_desc]
那名军官又来到了层云堡，一下车就怒气冲冲地走到了市政厅门前，还没等守卫开口，他就直接将一张纸拍在了守卫的脸上：“长眼睛了吗？看见了吗？这儿！女皇的亲笔签名！能不能进？我能不能进？”
守卫没说什么，让开了道，军官走了进去，看到了桌前的喷火：“喷火，这次是女皇陛下亲自发出的邀请函，叫你去皇宫面谈征兵事宜。”
说完，军官又小声嘟囔道：“哼！就这种小垃圾堡，都不该有面见女皇的资格。”
喷火在桌前写着文件，头也不抬地说道：“好的邮差，谢谢，你把邀请函放在桌上，我会去的。走之前记得把门带上。”

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_4_o0]
额...

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_5]
从层云堡到坎特洛特

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_5_desc]
列车正在缓缓驶入坎特洛特，坐在特殊车厢窗边的喷火，略感紧张，但并不慌乱。
喷火很清楚，女皇这次邀请她参加的并不是一次会面，而是一场陷阱。在离开层云堡之前，喷火已经向所有居民发布了通告，告诉他们自己将前往坎特洛特，如果没能回来，那么起义将会立刻爆发，无法停止，直到层云堡的最后一名居民被帝国军队杀死。这便是层云堡的秘密武器——团结。喷火信任层云堡的居民，她相信他们会坚守自己的立场，而这种抵抗到底的威慑，就足以让帝国军队望而却步。
帝国想要的是什么？帝国并不需要层云堡的资源，也不需要在层云堡征兵，帝国需要的是一个榜样，一个示范，一个帝国有能力控制和逼迫自己的领土按照中央意愿行事的证明。一方面，这意味着如果有必要，帝国一定会将他们的威慑贯彻到底，否则层云堡对帝国的拒绝将成为各个领地效仿的对象。但另一方面，这也意味着层云堡孱弱的威慑变得强大：即使层云堡一定会输，如果层云堡与帝国镇压的军队血战到最后一刻，这种代价以及舆论影响，对帝国来说也是无法承受的。
所以，只要冲突的代价双方都无法接受，这就一场鹰鸽博弈，一场勇敢者的游戏。而喷火坚信层云堡将会胜利的原因也就明显了——喷火比和煦的意志更加坚定，层云堡的居民比帝国的政府更团结，更勇敢。这就足矣让小小的层云堡与帝国这个庞然大物平起平坐了。

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_5_o0]
那就来聊聊

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_6]
勇敢者的游戏

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_6_desc]
“喷火，你应该已经看过帝国陆军的‘邮差’递给你的文件了吧？” 喷火走进房间，还不等献上层云堡的特产，女皇就开门见山地问道。
“是的，女皇陛下。那么您应该也已经看过我出发前在层云堡发布的通告了吧？” 喷火微微一笑，将包中拿出的特产放在了一边。

“我看过了，” 女皇点点头，“你的通告很有趣，‘战争期间，层云堡居民应全力支持小马利亚帝国。如果在层云堡发现任何脱离前线的帝国逃兵，层云堡居民们应誓死拦截，交给女皇陛下处理’。挺好笑的对吧？‘脱离前线的帝国逃兵’？” 女皇讽刺道。
“女皇陛下，通告的重点是‘层云堡居民应全力支持小马利亚帝国’。您可以不用多想。” 喷火点点头，微笑着说道，“我相信层云堡的居民一定会坚守自己的立场，不负女皇陛下的期望，消灭每一名逃兵，直到最后一刻。”
“很不错！层云堡是如此的忠诚，我都在考虑，战争胜利以后让层云堡从帝国完全独立呢！” 和煦光流试探性地说道，看着喷火的反应。喷火则反应迅速：“我们怎么会想要从女皇陛下的英明统治中独立呢？您看，正是陛下您的保护，让我们免于战争之苦，直到现在层云堡都没有小马被送上战场。”

眼见喷火继续阴阳怪气，和煦光流女皇新起了一个话题：“哦对了，喷火，不知道你有没有在层云堡的小餐馆里听到些风声。现在帝国征兵的待遇又要提高了，每个参军的小马能获得整整一车金币。” 随后，她凑到喷火身边，小声地说：“其实，待遇提高的不止有士兵。你知道吗，每个征兵表现优秀的天马自治领，市长都会得到一笔不菲的奖励。你说，这是不是个不错的机会呢？”
“女皇陛下，” 喷火看着和煦光流，“我担任自治领的市长，是因为层云堡的居民信任我，相信我一定能全心全意服务帝国，而不是贪图钱财。”
“对，喷火你说的对。” 贿赂不成，和煦光流又继续说道，“不过，这些奖励不止是给市长的，我最近在考虑将层云堡的补贴比例提高到7%。喷火，你觉得这个提议怎么样？或者，10%呢？”
“女皇陛下，” 喷火再次摇摇头：“层云堡地方比较小，最缺乏的是劳动力，参加军队影响了对帝国建设事业的贡献，是百分之几的补贴无法弥补的。”

“那先不聊这个，” 和煦光流女皇的语气中透露出她强压着的怒火：“你来参加这次会面是我邀请的，所以我也会保护你的安全。但现在这个局势也是非常危险的，你要小心，将来哪一天，在层云堡，别出什么意外。比如被抵抗组织刺杀什么的。”
喷火听出了女皇的意思，却还是微笑着回复：“感谢女皇的关心！我都会随身携带武器保护自己安全的。即使我遭遇不测，“自由层云堡”的同志也一定会很快找出凶手，让他们付出代价的。以牙还牙，以眼还眼，这是我们的原则，哪怕是在坎特洛特活动的‘抵抗组织’，也不例外。” 说着，喷火整理了整理衣服，不经意间露出侧身包中的武器——虽然它们已经经过帝国检查，但这还是让女皇下意识地后腿了几步。

和煦光流肉眼可见地有些慌张，沉默许久，喝了一口茶压惊：“喷火。你可以走了。”
“谢谢女皇陛下，所以说征兵的事情？” 喷火继续拍了拍她侧身的包。
“层云堡不仅不需要征兵，我还要奖励你们的忠诚，” 和煦光流女皇颤抖着说道，“奖励市长的那几车金币、层云堡补贴、以及战争胜利后的独立，我都会给你们的。”

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_6_o0]
“诶？” 连喷火也有些意外。

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_7]
从坎特洛特到层云堡

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_7_desc]
喷火离开后，女皇房间的一扇暗门打开，花花短裤从阴影中走了出来，一边拍着蹄子一边称赞道：“多么精彩的表演啊，女皇陛下，您真是太厉害了！”
和煦光流也恢复到了原本傲慢的模样，“是花花短裤你的剧本写得好，我只是按照你的剧本演出而已。不过，你确定这样就能奏效么？”

入夜，层云堡对面的小餐馆里，庆祝的声音几乎要将屋顶掀翻。居民们本已经做好了最坏的打算——喷火可能没法活着回来，层云堡将与帝国军队爆发正面冲突。如今，不仅没有冲突，层云堡还从帝国那里得到了不少的好处，包括提升的7%补贴，以及战后的独立地位。这一切都是喷火的功劳，层云堡的居民们都在为喷火的胜利而庆祝。
流言沙沙则继续坐在角落里喝着酒，当有小马到他的桌前坐下的时候，他就会小声说几句：“你说，伟大的喷火究竟是怎么做到的呢？听喷火自己说，和煦光流态度180度大转弯，完全答应了她的条件，这怎么可能呢？我听到传闻说，和煦给了喷火一些个体的好处，有好几车金币呢，现在就停在市政厅后面。还有传言说是和煦给的是10%的补贴，而不是7%，剩下3%好像是喷火要求给自己的。你说，这是真的么？”
流言沙沙知道这里是层云堡最热闹的地方，一句话，就足够改变整座城镇的思想。

[zh.EVENT_C01_C04_REDSKY_7_o0]
共苦易，同甘难
